# repro 2 (numeric module id): Grocery active, link ...?id=628&page=item&module=3
before=1 after=3 ; log: "route: initial route module=3" -> "module match found=true for slug=3" (no "deferring" on this pass) ; Back -> Home renders Pharmacy (grocery markers 0, pharmacy markers 5)

# control (NEARS-2738 contract): Grocery active, plain STORE link /store/mediquick-pharmacy-abu-dhabi?id=55&page=store&module=pharmacy
before=1 after=1 ; only the store-route pass runs ("deferring to StoreScreen store-scoped resolution") ; Back -> Home still Grocery
=> the switch comes from the extra `initial` GetPage pass that only the item-link success path triggers.

# likely mechanism (code read, worktree @354f0e03a):
# link_converter_helper.dart success path: Get.offAllNamed(RouteHelper.getInitialRoute()) then Get.toNamed/offNamed(storeRoute)
#   storeRoute = getStoreRoute(..., moduleId: <raw link param>, fromDeeplink: true)  -> '?...&module=<B>&from_deeplink=true'
# route_helper.dart:561-580 `initial` GetPage reads Get.parameters['module'] / ['from_deeplink'] -> log shows module=<B> (not the
#   grocery-food slug getInitialRoute() was built with), so _waitForModule -> checkModuleId(allowOutOfZoneRelocate=false) takes the
#   `foundModule != null` branch (route_helper.dart:1705-1718): ModuleController.setModule(B) + updateHeader + HomeController.loadData(true).
# Pre-fix this branch was unreachable cross-module (the fetch 404'd first), so the fix newly exposes it.
